<title>USA: Clinton calls Dole to tell him of Iraq strike.</title>
<headline>Clinton calls Dole to tell him of Iraq strike.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>President Clinton Tuesday telephoned Republican rival Bob Dole, a critic of his dealings with Iraqi leader Saddam Hussein, and told him about the decision to launch a missile attack on targets in Iraq.</p>
<p>&quot;The president thought it was a very good call,&quot; White House Press Secretary Mike McCurry said, declining to elaborate on the conversation.</p>
</text>
